## What changed

- adds a WebGL 2 voxel renderer that works on GitHub Pages;
- loads GLSL ES 3.00 vertex and fragment shaders from resource files;
- adds perspective and debug-camera view matrices;
- renders one grass cube and one rock cube in one indexed aggregate mesh and one draw call;
- adds original generated grass and rock atlas tiles with nearest-neighbor filtering;
- enables depth testing, back-face culling, and basic per-face brightness attributes;
- explicitly disposes VAOs, VBOs, EBOs, texture, program, shaders, and camera listeners;
- adds atlas, mesh-index, winding, projection, and view-matrix tests;
- strengthens Chromium smoke tests to require visible non-sky geometry and zero WebGL errors;
- updates both GitHub Pages entry paths and documentation.

## Scope boundaries

No terrain, chunks, caves, collision, world generation, player physics, block breaking, or placement were added. The Java desktop target remains a Phase 1 reference; Phase 2 is implemented in the public WebGL 2 target so it runs in browsers.

## Validation

CI runs the existing Java build and desktop smoke test, checks every browser module, runs all Node tests, loads both Pages entry points in Chromium, compiles the shaders, renders the indexed mesh, and verifies one draw call, zero WebGL errors, and visible geometry.

## What changed

- make `Write-GodotLabMcpConfig.ps1` share the governed path-policy primitives used by Windows estate acceptance;
- repair the shared `Assert-NoReparsePoint` primitive so it walks regular-file and directory ancestors portably instead of assuming every filesystem item has a `.Parent` property;
- reject Lab, allowed-target, evidence and managed-engine overlap before creating evidence or engine directories;
- require absolute evidence, engine and output paths;
- require `OutputPath` to remain strictly beneath `EvidenceRoot` before any directory creation and after canonical resolution;
- reject reparse-point traversal for the Lab, Python executable, target roots, managed roots, output parent and existing output;
- preserve and deduplicate every configured target root in the generated MCP arguments;
- write UTF-8 without BOM through a same-directory temporary file;
- allow replacement only when the existing file is a strict standalone generated Godot Lab `mcpServers` snippet with the same server name;
- refuse to overwrite arbitrary or combined client configuration;
- add executable PowerShell regression tests for evidence overlap, engine overlap, output escape, multi-root propagation, offline/noninteractive flags, safe refresh and arbitrary-config preservation.

## Root causes

1. The standalone config writer was weaker than the installer and worker paths. It created `EvidenceRoot` and `EngineRoot` before complete isolation checks, never validated `EvidenceRoot`, used prefix-only engine checks and allowed `OutputPath` anywhere on disk.
2. It overwrote an existing file even though the runbook states that client configuration is not overwritten implicitly.
3. The shared reparse guard used `.Parent` on the result of `Get-Item`; that is not portable for regular files and would fail when validating Python executables, strict JSON files and other file evidence.

## Exact scope

Base: `2e70ed00d718168b52ae20212c33849bd004b852`.

Exactly three production paths change:

```text
scripts/GodotLabEstateAcceptance.Common.ps1
scripts/Write-GodotLabMcpConfig.ps1
tests/test_windows_mcp_config_root_policy.py
```

No workflow, target-game source, deployment, credential, publication, arbitrary shell or physical-controller authority is introduced.

## Validation

The public CI lane must pass repository authority, adversarial fixtures, pinned dependencies and MCP identity, Python compilation, managed-engine policy, Ruff, Bash and PowerShell parsing, the complete pytest suite including the new live `pwsh` tests, wheel construction and clean-source verification.

The first two candidate runs usefully exposed test and shared-path defects before merge: one passed a symlinked hosted Python executable; the next proved the shared file-ancestor walk was not portable. Both were corrected on the branch rather than bypassed.

## Truth boundary

This protects source and client configuration during MCP setup. It does not prove Greg's physical Windows desktop, GPU, sound devices, games or connected MCP client completed physical estate acceptance.

